{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-009", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Korea to fund $274 million into a new display research platform, focused on OLED and post-OLED technologies", "content": "<p>The South Korean government has approved a new national display R&amp;D project, the Advanced Display National Research Platform. The project, run by the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Resources (MOTIR), will start in 2027 and run for seven years, with a total budget of around $274 million, of which $207 million will come from the national budget. The project has now passed its preliminary feasibility study, the review that large public R&amp;D projects in Korea must pass before they are fun", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/korea-approves-274-million-national-display-research-platform-focused-oled-and", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-06-010", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec", "lg_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["samsung_elec", "lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["panel_price", "oled_penetration", "it_panel_demand"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "LG Display targets China's internet cafes with WOLED gaming panels, days after Samsung's QD-OLED cafe program", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-oled\">LG Display</a> says that it is expanding its supply of WOLED gaming monitor panels in China, as local monitor brands chase the country's fast-growing internet cafes and gaming hotels. LGD is working with ANTGAMER, the gaming brand of Chinese panel maker <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/hkc\">HKC</a>, on its internet cafe business, and it also works with AOC, ViewSonic and ASUS in China.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/mcp-", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-targets-chinas-internet-cafes-woled-gaming-panels-days-after", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-011", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Commentary: US governors target AI data centers as Taiwan firms await Nvidia outlook", "content": "Following the 2026 US gubernatorial elections, four states that host major AI data centers&mdash;Texas, Ohio, Georgia, and Pennsylvania&mdash;could impose tighter controls on new projects after Democratic candidates won or secured reelection, according to <em>Bloomberg</em>. Taiwan suppliers are watching closely as some projects could be paused, while Nvidia's upcoming earnings call is expected to provide clues on AI infrastructure demand.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261106PD241/usa-data-center-ai-outlook-2026.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-012", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Wistron ITS reports record third-quarter profit as AI and semiconductor focus accelerates", "content": "Wistron ITS reported record gross profit, operating profit, net income, and earnings per share in the third quarter of 2026, as stronger revenue and improved operating efficiency supported continued expansion in AI and semiconductor services. Consolidated revenue reached NT$3.752 billion (approx. US$114.1 million), up 3.5% quarter-over-quarter and 25.6% year-over-year.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261106PD234/wistron-its-revenue-profit-growth.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-013", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "mass production"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "EOI posts record nine-month results, readies Mexico plant for 4Q26 production", "content": "Excellence Opto (EOI), a major automotive LED light-source supplier, posted record revenue and profit for the first nine months as product-mix optimization, supply-chain efficiencies and high global capacity utilization lifted results. The company is also preparing to begin mass production at its Mexico plant in the fourth quarter and to develop SiPh optical communication module samples by 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261106PD233/eoi-mexico-production-plant-excellence-opto.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-014", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.67, "keywords": ["loss", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "LX Semicon posts first quarterly operating loss since IPO", "content": "South Korean chip designer LX Semicon posted its first quarterly operating loss since going public in 2010, as weak demand for display chips and pricing pressure from electronics manufacturers weighed on earnings. The company also nominated a new CEO to lead its turnaround efforts.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261106VL212/lx-semicon-loss-semicon-display-revenue.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-015", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["panel_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "TV panel makers hold prices firm in November despite fading demand, with supply cuts proving crucial", "content": "The global TV panel market entered a period of fragile equilibrium in November 2026 following the end of peak-season inventory replenishment. Although TV brands have become more cautious in procurement, panel manufacturers are adjusting production at advanced-generation LCD fabs to stabilize prices, with rising upstream material costs reinforcing their reluctance to offer discounts.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261106PD232/tv-panel-demand-market-production-tv.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-016", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "China's NSIG sees silicon wafer prices rebound, but profitability remains elusive", "content": "National Silicon Industry Group (NSIG) expects to complete its expansion to 1.2 million 300mm silicon wafers per month by the end of 2026, positioning the Chinese semiconductor materials supplier to benefit from recovering wafer prices and growing demand for silicon-on-insulator (SOI) substrates used in silicon photonics (SiPh).", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261106VL208/nsig-silicon-wafer-300mm-expansion.html", "type": "rss"}]}
